          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On March 23, 2022, at 10:08 PM, a resident of LACOUR-D’ARCENAY (21) observes the sky and hears a deep, humming noise. Suddenly, the object appears from the south, flying almost vertically over the witness's location, and continues in a northeasterly direction before turning towards northwest. The object appears to be at low altitude. Three blue lights are visible (one in the center, two \"spaced out,\" possibly on the wings?). The case consistency is average: one witness, no photos or videos. The description of PAN strongly resembles the observation of a military aircraft, an explanation the witness himself favors. The CNOA (National Center for Aerial Operations of the Air and Space Force) report requested by GEIPAN confirms that PAN corresponds to a military aircraft in visual flight, based on the trajectory, timing, and location (see the investigation report). The case is classified as A, observation of a military aircraft.",
